From: Xios Project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Export AbortWithReasonSPI for GTK builds on Darwin

Assertions.h includes AbortWithReasonSPI.h whenever the target is Darwin, but
the GTK port's Darwin header list does not copy it into the generated WTF
include tree. Export it alongside the other Darwin SPI headers so
JavaScriptCore's build-time tools can compile against that tree.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformGTK.cmake
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux")
     )
 elseif (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Darwin")
     list(APPEND WTF_PUBLIC_HEADERS
+        spi/darwin/AbortWithReasonSPI.h
         spi/darwin/OSVariantSPI.h
         spi/darwin/ProcessMemoryFootprint.h
     )
